From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] touch/focaltech: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(touch/focaltech: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/touch/focaltech to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - relax -Wmissing-prototypes (on by default since 6.8, fatal with CONFIG_WERROR) for this vendor code

Files: ft3658/BUILD.bazel, ft3658/focaltech_core.c, ft3658/focaltech_test/focaltech_test.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * drm_bridge_funcs lost the non-atomic .enable/.disable. The panel bridge
    uses .atomic_enable/.atomic_disable (same bodies; they get the commit
    and ignore it) plus the bridge-state helpers the atomic hooks require.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      ft3658/Kbuild
---
diff --git a/ft3658/BUILD.bazel b/ft3658/BUILD.bazel
index 7e9c65f..6f32a8d 100644
